Subject: Load the original common.ini and datetime.ini at start
Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84

The original main loads ini/common.ini into Config::Global() and waits for
ini/datetime.ini (the /General/Build Info tweaks) before the task loop. The
block stayed behind the early MSCHARGED_DIAGNOSTIC_MAIN_BOOTSTRAP gate, so the
full game never loaded it and every common.ini value used its default: goal
replays placed their generic cameras at 0,0,0 (always the same low angle,
reported by a user), and demo-mode timeouts, popup spacing and transition
fades used built-in values. Admit the original block with the frontend
sequence, like its neighbours; the source is unchanged.

diff --git a/src/Game/main.cpp b/src/Game/main.cpp
index cffdba0..350392c 100644
--- a/src/Game/main.cpp
+++ b/src/Game/main.cpp
@@ -598,7 +598,7 @@ static void Initialize()
     }
 #endif // original shared material textures; named world draw keeps this exact request
 
-#if !defined(MSCHARGED_DIAGNOSTIC_MAIN_BOOTSTRAP)
+#if !defined(MSCHARGED_DIAGNOSTIC_MAIN_BOOTSTRAP) || defined(MSCHARGED_DIAGNOSTIC_FRONTEND_SEQUENCE)
     u8 temporaryState = lbl_806E1458;
     ParticleUpdateNoOp(&temporaryState);
 
